{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507180-ways-for-a-ghoul-to-get-around-bypass-the-blood-bond","id":1507180,"title":"Ways for a ghoul to get around / bypass the blood bond?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-02T07:09:19-07:00","id":1507180,"title":"Ways for a ghoul to get around / bypass the blood bond?","content":"<b><i>It's just a tought exercise. Like writing a novel. Not intended to be used in a real game.</i></b><br /> <br /> <br /> So, here's the issue: let's say there is an occultist / hunter / would-be-ghoul who knows fairly well the potential and dangers offered by Vitae.<br /> He's a mortal, but a very skilled, very trained and obscenely motivated one. Years of studying, research, physical conditioning, martial arts, weapon pratice... within the limits of a human being he's very capable. <br /> <br /> He's also completely ruthless. He captured a couple young vampires, locked them in his survivalist bunker hidden deep in the woods and interrogated them for months or even years. He performed experiments and tested every kind of folk lore about vampires on them ( garlic, crosses, spread rice ecc. ) so he could discern true lore from superstitious garbage. Feed them both human and animal blood, tested their limits, got an idea about Vitae basic powers, even forced them to create ghouls out of animals ( dogs, rats ecc. ) and recorded the changes which the Vitae apport to living beings.<br /> <br /> In short, he knows about vampirism all that can be reasonably discovered through extensive experimentation.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> The occultist goal is to achieve the good things that come from being a ghoul ( eternal youth, unhuman strength and resilience, healing powers and the exhilarating rush of Vitae ) without becoming a vampire's slave.<br /> So, there's any reasonable ( I mean &quot;not exceedingly improbable and difficult&quot; ) way to get around the problem of blood bond?<br /> <br /> The simplest way I thought is quite cruel and brutal, but may be effective: the occultist may utterly destroy - physically and mentally - a prisoner vampire through prolonged torture and mutilation taking care to not outright kill him, then - when he's absolutely sure the poor thing is utterly helpless and catatonic, use the vampire's Vitae and get bonded.<br /> He keeps his &quot;master&quot; into his bunker feeding him pig blood and taking Vitae from him when needed, and the vampire is unable to give orders of any kind.<br /> <br /> Other ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T08:44:47-07:00","id":1507188,"title":"","content":"Rather than going catatonic, I would expect the victim of such prolonged and extreme torture to descend into wrightdom. That's going to create some pretty major difficulties with ensuring the vampire now effectively locked in perpetual frenzy remains properly fed, and problems with getting that vampire's blood. It might work for awhile, maybe even a few decades, but I'd expect that eventually the ghoul's love for the vampire would cause that ghoul to slip up, make a mistake and get turned into the wright's snack at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T12:21:47-07:00","id":1507194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507180-ways-for-a-ghoul-to-get-around-bypass-the-blood-bond#post1507180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>It's just a tought exercise. Like writing a novel. Not intended to be used in a real game.</i></b><br /> <br /> <br /> So, here's the issue: let's say there is an occultist / hunter / would-be-ghoul who knows fairly well the potential and dangers offered by Vitae.<br /> He's a mortal, but a very skilled, very trained and obscenely motivated one. Years of studying, research, physical conditioning, martial arts, weapon pratice... within the limits of a human being he's very capable.<br /> <br /> He's also completely ruthless. He captured a couple young vampires, locked them in his survivalist bunker hidden deep in the woods and interrogated them for months or even years. He performed experiments and tested every kind of folk lore about vampires on them ( garlic, crosses, spread rice ecc. ) so he could discern true lore from superstitious garbage. Feed them both human and animal blood, tested their limits, got an idea about Vitae basic powers, even forced them to create ghouls out of animals ( dogs, rats ecc. ) and recorded the changes which the Vitae apport to living beings.<br /> <br /> In short, he knows about vampirism all that can be reasonably discovered through extensive experimentation.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> The occultist goal is to achieve the good things that come from being a ghoul ( eternal youth, unhuman strength and resilience, healing powers and the exhilarating rush of Vitae ) without becoming a vampire's slave.<br /> So, there's any reasonable ( I mean &quot;not exceedingly improbable and difficult&quot; ) way to get around the problem of blood bond?<br /> <br /> The simplest way I thought is quite cruel and brutal, but may be effective: the occultist may utterly destroy - physically and mentally - a prisoner vampire through prolonged torture and mutilation taking care to not outright kill him, then - when he's absolutely sure the poor thing is utterly helpless and catatonic, use the vampire's Vitae and get bonded.<br /> He keeps his &quot;master&quot; into his bunker feeding him pig blood and taking Vitae from him when needed, and the vampire is unable to give orders of any kind.<br /> <br /> Other ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this idea has already been used. Other than that it doesn't have a quality that allows you to do just that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T13:08:32-07:00","id":1507202,"title":"","content":"the first couple of ideas that come to mind would be.<br /> <br /> 1) the occultist kills the vampire after drinking the blood, I can't recall if Vitae retains it's power if the vampire it belong to perishes if it does then our man can keep a few vials of Vitae to maintain his ghouldom for a time and then use the last vial to turn some poor soul into a vampire and start the cycle again.<br /> <br /> 2) the occultist happens to to be one of few rare individuals who are unboundable.<br /> <br /> 3) using superpowers to break any blood bonds he might get from drinking Vitae, now of course breaking a blood oath is going to require serious power which our occultist being just a ghoul will be unable to obtain on his own therefore he will have to ask outside help from someone like a mage.<br /> <br /> 4) the occultist has or develops an iron will towards the blood bond, if the occultist knows everything the curse of caine then he would know that any positive feelings he has towards his kindred captive are false and just has overcome them though sheer will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27369,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","user":"The smiling gun-knight","date":". 04-02-2023, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","name":"The smiling gun-knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T14:03:40-07:00","id":1507208,"title":"","content":"I believe there was a group described in Ghoul: Fatal Addiction that was made up of ghouls who wanted the benefits of vitae without being enslaved by the vampire. They were basically a group of hunters who would stalk vampires, capture them, drain them of blood for future use, and then destroy the vampire before they ever ingested their vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T14:05:35-07:00","id":1507209,"title":"","content":"If I remember well, Vitae decays fairly fast but there are rituals to keep it &quot;fresh&quot;, rituals that an occultist / sorcerer / hedge magician may or may not be able to discover.<br /> <br /> Breaking the blood bond once it forms looks like a very long shot to me, but mabye an occultist could <i>prevent</i> the bond from forming, mabye distillating the Vitae into an elixir.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe there was a group described in Ghoul: Fatal Addiction that was made up of ghouls who wanted the benefits of vitae without being enslaved by the vampire. They were basically a group of hunters who would stalk vampires, capture them, drain them of blood for future use, and then destroy the vampire before they ever ingested their vitae. </div> </div> </div>This is risky and a lot of work...<br /> although there's a major advantage: if a group capture a vampire, force-feeds him animal blood and take his Vitae ( probably extracting it from the heart with a syringe ), a single vampire captive could provide Vitae for 10 or even 100 ghouls - even if only for a month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 04-02-2023, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}